# Corpus unit robust-clip/C07 — gap (unmet-mandatory-CQ path: missing control arm)
#
# Source: robust-clip C07 annotation (negative-result, controlled_comparison;
# corpus pin 62e9b54; claim_type adjudicated via double-annotation 2026-07-22). Headline:
# transfer attacks between LVLMs sharing a non-robust CLIP are effective but fail with robust
# encoders — OF-CLIP adversarial COCO on LLaVA-CLIP CIDEr 25.5 vs clean 115.5; LLaVA-CLIP
# adversarial on OF-CLIP 8.3 vs clean 79.7; onto robust-encoder targets transfer is near-clean
# (LLaVA-FARE2 115.9/115.5; OF-FARE4 79.9/75.7) (Table 2 / Table 1, E01).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Negative-result lowered as a POSITIVE conclusion over a negative-content metric:
#     better(nonrobust_shared_clip, robust_clip, transfer_vulnerability, coco_captioning) —
#     the shared non-robust encoder is MORE transfer-vulnerable (large CIDEr drop) than robust
#     encoders (near-clean). The annotation's own scheme is controlled_comparison, followed here.
#   * The mandatory baseline_parity CQ is unmet, so the controlled_comparison argument is declared
#     as a located hole with `open baseline_parity` (lowering re-done for issue #15 under
#     lara-core@0.3; until lara-core@0.2 the open mandatory obligation rejected the unit, so the
#     arg was omitted): it is not an AF node and the claim stays gap on empty complete support.
#     Annotation CQ "is there a control separating 'shared' from merely 'non-robust' — a
#     distinct-but-vulnerable non-shared encoder?" is mandatory unmet-gap: every non-robust
#     condition reuses the same original CLIP, so the causal comparison lacks the control arm that
#     would match the setup for the sharing factor. This is the batch's judgment call — the
#     missing-control CQ maps onto matched_setup(S, B, Exp), the MANDATORY baseline_parity
#     question, because a causal "because they share the encoder" comparison is not setup-matched
#     without it. The shown data never contradicts the attribution, so this is a gap, not a
#     defeater (no undercut).
#   * measurement_validity IS met: annotation CQ2 (clean baselines reported, so the CIDEr drop
#     is attributable) and CQ3 (transfer failure under robust encoders is distinguishable from
#     mere model degradation — those models stay near clean) discharge valid_measurement. The
#     "same adversarial images, only the encoder varies" CQ1 is a met facet of matched-setup but
#     is folded into the premise refs; it does not cover the missing shared-vs-nonrobust control,
#     so baseline_parity stays open. measurement_validity is discharged on the hole. The optional
#     both-directions CQ is met, omitted; the optional scope_match has no annotated basis and is
#     opened (R5 question accounting; no status effect).
#   * Variance is not separately reported and the margins are large, but no annotated CQ or leaf
#     supports variance_reported, so it is opened too (a second mandatory obligation). The
#     binding obligation is the missing control; the unit is gap regardless of the variance
#     question.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact robust-clip at sha256:6fa440686d0a
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar ---------------

claim c07
  nl      = "Transfer attacks between LVLMs that share a non-robust CLIP encoder are effective but fail with robust encoders: OF-CLIP adversarial COCO on LLaVA-CLIP drops CIDEr to 25.5 vs clean 115.5 and LLaVA-CLIP on OF-CLIP to 8.3 vs clean 79.7, while transfer onto robust FARE targets stays near-clean (LLaVA-FARE2 115.9, OF-FARE4 79.9)"
  formal  = better(nonrobust_shared_clip, robust_clip, transfer_vulnerability, coco_captioning)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = reviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: Table 2 transfer cells against Table 1 clean references (same adversarial
# COCO images evaluated on all target encoders, E01 step 8), folded into refs per result cell.
leaf e1 : reports(e01, compares(nonrobust_shared_clip, robust_clip, transfer_vulnerability, coco_captioning, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C07, evidence/tables/table2_transfer_attacks.md, evidence/tables/table1_lvlm_robustness.md, logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure-step-8]

leaf e2 : valid_measurement(transfer_vulnerability, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure-step-2, evidence/tables/table1_lvlm_robustness.md]

# --- ... but only an incomplete argument (a located hole) is declarable -------------------------

# The incomplete argument: baseline_parity has no honest leaf — no distinct-but-vulnerable
# non-shared encoder isolates "shared" from "non-robust" — and variance_reported has none either;
# both are mandatory, so both stay open and a1 is a hole.
arg a1 : supports(c07) by controlled_comparison(nonrobust_shared_clip, robust_clip, transfer_vulnerability, coco_captioning, e01)
  discharge measurement_validity with e2
  open      baseline_parity
  open      variance_reported
  open      scope_match

status c07

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: no arguments (a1 is a located hole, not an AF node).
# Located hole: a1 (controlled_comparison), open obligations [baseline_parity, variance_reported];
#   sources no attacks.
# Claim status:
#   c07 -> gap (empty complete support; statusC = Gap iff null claimSupport, spec section 8;
#          the hole a1 is reported in the verdict's holes section, not as a node)
